    "narrative": "With the Austin Waves pushing for every marginal gain in our 5x5 Roto chase, today\u2019s board is anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who clocks in as our top play with a 74.56 score. Facing Feltner (4.98 xERA), **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against a pitcher struggling with high-contact profiles, and his placement in the #4 hole provides the RBI floor we desperately need. **Drake Baldwin** follows closely with a 69.17 rating; his role as a leadoff hitter against Martinez (4.65 xERA) creates a high-ceiling environment for run production, capitalizing on the SP\u2019s inability to limit baserunners early in counts.\n\nThe secondary tier presents a more cautious outlook, as both **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci** draw a tough assignment against Jones (3.57 xERA). While **Sam Antonacci** manages a 48.61 score thanks to his leadoff status and speed profile\u2014critical for our scarcity-driven strategy\u2014the matchup keeps his efficiency in the marginal range. **Dominic Smith** is our most interesting bench-adjacent start today; with a score of 58.04, he narrowly missed the \"Strong\" threshold but remains in the lineup due to his platoon edge against the righty Martinez. While **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are all unavailable today due to schedule gaps, and **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, we are closely monitoring the bottom of the roster. **Nasim Nunez** and **Wade Meckler** remain on high alert should any late-inning defensive replacements or unexpected lineup shuffles require us to swap in additional speed to keep our SB volume competitive.",
